  <wpt lat="34.462430" lon="-120.048300">
    <ele>11.0</ele>
    <name>Refugio SB - NIGHT 2 (hike/bike)</name>
    <desc>NIGHT 2 (if booking rather than camping wild). 10 Refugio Beach Road, Goleta CA 93117 - 20 miles west of Santa Barbara, off US-101 at Refugio Road. Hike-and-bike campsites confirmed; drinking water, restrooms, showers, outdoor showers, and a camp store on site. Open August 2026. Park/district phone (805) 968-1033. VERIFY the per-person hike/bike rate: the $10/person figure in the plan is NOT published on the park page - phone it. SRC parks.ca.gov/refugio  [day2_limekiln_refugio km 280]</desc>
    <sym>Campground</sym>
    <type>camp</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.460000" lon="-120.024000">
    <ele>11.0</ele>
    <name>El Capitan SB - NIGHT 2 alt (3 km later)</name>
    <desc>Third of the three Gaviota-coast hike/bike parks, 2.6 km east of Refugio, and the one with the most services. Reported first-come, first-served on the middle/upper loops through 28 Jun 2026 - VERIFY current status and whether that extends to August.  [day2_limekiln_refugio km 280, 2250 m off route]</desc>
    <sym>Campground</sym>
    <type>camp</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.461000" lon="-120.036000">
    <ele>11.0</ele>
    <name>INFO Aniso Trail - paved path El Capitan &lt;-&gt; Refugio</name>
    <desc>A 2.5 mile undulating paved bike path along the bluff between El Capitan and Refugio - the pleasant way to start day 3 instead of the 101 shoulder. A segment has been closed for storm damage; VERIFY on site, and drop back onto 101 if it is shut.  [day2_limekiln_refugio km 280, 1145 m off route]</desc>
    <sym>Bike Trail</sym>
    <type>info</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.462430" lon="-120.048300">
